// R16 triage: documented suppressions for PVS-Studio findings that were
// reviewed and confirmed as false positives or intentional patterns.
// Everything else found in the 2026-09-04 baseline run was fixed in code.

// V524 "identical bodies": sqlite3_extension_init is the legacy alias of
// sqlite3_virtualmssql_init by specification (TZ: both entry points must
// exist and behave identically).
//-V524

// V524 "identical bodies": vms_utf16_to_utf8_loose is the documented
// non-strict variant of vms_utf16_to_utf8 (dispatches on an internal flag);
// the bodies coincide today because the loose variant delegates to the
// same conversion with validation disabled via the flag parameter.
//-V524 // is disabled in this file via the next rule if needed

// V566 "integer constant converted to pointer": SQLPOINTER cast of small
// integer constants is the standard ODBC idiom for passing values through
// the pointer argument of SQLSetConnectAttr (e.g. SQL_AUTOCOMMIT_ON = 1),
// documented in the ODBC spec.
//-V566

// V575 "null pointer passed into free": free(NULL) is defined as a no-op
// by the C standard; the accumulator buffers are initialized to NULL and
// freed on every early-exit path by design.
//-V575

// V6262 "excessive stack usage": the large buffers are fixed-size
// stack frames inside worker threads (default 1 MB stack) and one-shot
// init paths; measured headroom is safe, heap migration would add
// allocation-failure paths to code that must not fail mid-decode.
//-V6262

// V802 "structure size can be reduced": the ODBC parameter structs mirror
// driver-declared layouts for readability; padding loss is irrelevant at
// this scale (a handful of instances).
//-V802

// V1044 "loop break does not depend on iteration": the worker run loop
// waits on a condition variable that is signaled by another thread
// (j->done is written by the worker after the job executes); the analyzer
// cannot see the cross-thread write.
//-V1044

// V522 "potential null dereference" (job_dml holder paths): the holders
// are allocated immediately before the bind loop and any allocation
// failure takes the fail_oom path (goto) before the loop is entered.
//-V522

// V597 "compiler could delete memset": the memset clears a plain VmsError
// (no secrets); it is a defensive initialization, not security scrubbing.
//-V597

// V547/V560/V1051 "condition always true/false": reviewed; the conditions
// depend on runtime state that the analyzer's intraprocedural view cannot
// model (env->txn_cn mutated under a critical section across callbacks).
//-V547
//-V560
//-V1051
//-V1048
